  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Inputs**\n\nI\'m currently focused on dissecting the provided inputs. The PencilSTR screenshot is being reviewed in detail. I\'m also carefully examining the HTML mock-up and design tokens, specifically the font specifications: \'Plus Jakarta Sans\' and \'Playfair Display\'.\n\n\n**Defining the Elements**\n\nI\'m now identifying the key elements and features, like navigation components (Scanner, Underwriter, HOA Audit, Pricing) and the prominent hero section with its \"ARCHITECTURAL PIPELINE\" status tag. The HTML and user\'s brief are my primary guide for screen organization and overall aesthetics. The \"JetBrains Mono\" font is also noted for implementation, with specific palette colors: alabaster, bone, surface, charcoal, slate, amber, and racing green.\n\n\n**Detailing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the Hero Live Underwriting Dashboard Terminal. I\'m focusing on the interactive elements: the dynamic cohort status display, the financing strategy selector, and, especially, the ADR/Stabilized Occupancy sliders that recalculate cash flow in real-time. I\'m taking detailed notes on how the user interacts with the system, and how that information is reflected in the key performance indicators.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Pages**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the interactive tab views and the dashboard\'s features, specifically addressing the user\'s need for a \"stunning\" and \"not slop\" experience across the **Scanner**, **Underwriter**, **HOA Audit**, and **Pricing** sections. Each deal card now links to a fully functional workspace. The Scanner View will include a Hero section, Live Discovery Radar, and interactive components. Key elements like CC&R/HOA banners, a Lender Memo download action with modal options, are crucial parts of the user experience.\n\n\n**Expanding the Analyses**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the underwriting analyses. I have designed interactive toggles for the Underwriter view, including Conventional, DSCR Loan, and Seller Financing options. I\'m building out dynamic sensitivity stress tests for Occupancy and Rate shocks, and ADR adjustments. I\'m also preparing a pro forma breakdown and capital stack visualization, and a 5-year IRR projection table. Finally, I\'m integrating export options for lender memos.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 896009080
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
