  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining App Components**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the app\'s components, starting with the header and navigation. I\'m focusing on the user features and screens to identify the required data structures and UI elements. Right now, I\'m specifically defining the elements within the header.\n\n\n**Designing Home View**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the Scanner/Home View. I envision a live architectural pipeline badge and an editorial headline to set the stage. An interactive search container will take center stage, allowing users to paste URLs or type addresses. I\'m including a \"Pencil Deal\" button with a scan animation to kickstart underwriting. Quick benchmarks of example properties will provide immediate context.\n\n\n**Visualizing Data Display**\n\nI\'m now detailing the hero dashboard terminal. I\'m focusing on the live scan cohort indicator, property details, and a projected revenue chart. I\'m envisioning the left sub-panel with property data and the right with financing strategies and key returns. I\'m prioritizing interactive elements for the revenue chart, allowing users to analyze monthly data.\n\n\n**Refining Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m currently refining the interactive elements for the financial dashboard. Specifically, I\'m focusing on incorporating real-time updating range sliders for Average Daily Rate and Stabilized Occupancy. As users adjust these, all key metrics, like Net NOI and DSCR, will dynamically update with smooth visual feedback. I\'m also adding an HOA CC&Rs banner with a warning and a clickable link to a full inspection drawer. Finally, a button to download a lender memo will be included.\n\n\n**Developing Underwriter Studio**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Underwriter Studio,\" which will be a full financial workstation. I\'m focusing on a strategy switcher to toggle between DSCR loans, conventional 30-year fixed, seller financing, and all strategies. I\'m envisioning three modules: DSCR & Creative Financing, a 100-page HOA & Zoning Scans module with a live clause audit checklist, and a pricing plan with interactive checkout. I\'m including audited case studies with an \"Open Full Underwrite\" action. Finally, I\'m adding an Obsidian bottom CTA banner and a minimalist footer.\n\n\n**Constructing Cash Flow**\n\nI\'m now building out the cash flow module. I\'m focusing on granular control of the capital stack, including purchase price, renovation budgets, and various interest rates. I\'m prioritizing the detailed pro forma ledger, which will include rental revenue, cleaning fees, platform fees, and property management fees. The goal is to provide a clear picture of Net Operating Income (NOI) and annual/monthly Net Cash Flow, culminating in critical metrics like Cash-on-Cash Return and DSCR.\n\n\n**Auditing STR Regulations**\n\nI\'m now detailing the HOA & CC&R Audit screen, a legal document analyzer specifically for short-term rental deed restrictions. I\'m focusing on the clause-by-clause AI audit findings. These include sections on rental permissibility, minimum night stays, parking regulations, noise restrictions, commercial activity interpretations, and municipal ordinance checks. The screen will display a Legal Risk Score and provide a recommended contract contingency clause.\n\n\n\n**Designing Report Tools**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive report tools. I\'m prioritizing the development of a lender memo modal, styled as a premium underwriting memorandum. It will include essential details like the deal reference, LTV, and debt yield. I\'m also planning batch report functionalities with options for deleting, editing, or printing.\n\nI\'m starting to build the backend with TypeScript files, specifically defining types in `src/types/index.ts`, creating mock deals in `src/data/mockDeals.ts`, and core financial calculations in `src/utils/calculator.ts`. I\'m building a streamlined `Navbar.tsx` component with active tab states and login modals.\n\n\n**Enumerating UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining the React components needed to construct the application. I\'m focusing on components, like `ScannerHero.tsx` for the initial scan view, and `UnderwriterStudio.tsx` for the full financial workstation. There is also `HoaAuditStudio.tsx` for CC&R analysis, and other essential modules like `PricingSection.tsx` for interactive pricing and `LenderMemoModal.tsx` for lender reports. I\'m ensuring an intuitive experience through modules such as `PipelineDrawer.tsx`, `CaseStudiesSection.tsx`, `FeatureModules.tsx`, `ObsidianCta.tsx`, and `Footer.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 11
      nanos: 338321535
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    provider_assigned_message_id: "fXe5at7OLumtz7IP_LTQ6A0"
  }
}
