  user_input {
    user_response: "Act as a Principal Full-Stack Engineer and Architect. You are building the complete authenticated application and backend systems for \"PencilSTR\" \342\200\224 an institutional-grade Short-Term Rental (STR) acquisition, underwriting, and portfolio management platform.\n\nThe public landing page is already completed. Your objective is to build the full logged-in user experience, the guest demo environment, and the robust backend services that power them.\n\n---\n\n### TECH STACK & SYSTEM CONSTRAINTS\n- **Frontend:** React 19 + Vite (TypeScript), Tailwind CSS, `@shadcn/ui`, `lucide-react`, `recharts` for financial visualizations, `@dnd-kit/core` for the Kanban CRM board, and `zustand` for client state.\n- **Backend / Edge Layer:** Node.js (Express or Hono) or Python (FastAPI). Clean service-layer pattern with typed request/response schemas.\n- **Database & Auth:** Supabase (PostgreSQL with RLS), Supabase Auth, and Supabase Storage for PDF document uploads.\n- **AI & Extraction Agents:** Gemini 2.5 Flash (via API) utilizing Structured JSON outputs for data extraction and long-context PDF analysis.\n- **External Integration Stubs & Providers:** Firecrawl API (URL web scraping), RentCast API (assessor and market rent benchmarks), Tavily API (autonomous market searches).\n- **Design Language:** Precision Architectural Light Mode. Warm bone/alabaster canvas (`#FAF9F6`), crisp white surfaces (`#FFFFFF`), hairline borders (`#E5E4DF`), charcoal text (`#111110`), racing green return metrics (`#0B3B24`), and rich amber warnings (`#D97706`).\n\n---\n\n### CORE ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n#### 1. Dual-Mode Authentication & Instant Guest Demo\n- [ ] Implement seamless standard authentication via Supabase Auth (Magic Link, Email/Password, and Google OAuth).\n- [ ] Implement a **1-Click Guest Demo Mode** accessible from the login screen:\n  - Initializes a temporary session or isolated sandbox environment without requiring email or payment.\n  - Automatically hydrates the database/client state with 3 fully realized pre-modeled deals across different markets:\n    1. *The Ridge Alpine* (4-Bed Gatlinburg Cabin, DSCR-financed, 19.4% CoC, Unrestricted HOA).\n    2. *Kierland Hideaway* (5-Bed Scottsdale Luxury Villa with Pool, Conventional, 17.1% CoC, Strict Noise Rules).\n    3. *Gulf Shores Sandcastle* (6-Bed Beachfront, Seller Financed / Creative, 22.8% CoC, HOA vehicle limits).\n  - Guest sessions can test every feature (sliders, Kanban moves, HOA document uploads, PDF memo downloads) with volatile state preserved in session storage or an ephemeral guest user row.\n\n#### 2. Backend API Services & Integration Pipelines\n- [ ] **URL Ingestion Endpoint (`POST /api/deals/ingest-url`):**\n  - Accepts a raw property URL (Zillow, Redfin, or brokerage listing).\n  - Uses Firecrawl (or mock scraper fallback) to extract the webpage markdown.\n  - Passes extracted markdown to Gemini 2.5 Flash with a strict JSON Schema returning: street address, city, state, zip, list price, beds, baths, sqft, year built, listed HOA fees, tax estimates, and photo URLs.\n  - Queries RentCast API (or regional valuation baseline) for assessed tax records and submarket Long-Term / STR rent index.\n  - Persists the new record into Supabase and returns a fully populated `Deal` object.\n- [ ] **Autonomous Market Sweep Engine (`POST /api/scanner/run-sweep` & Scheduled Cron):**\n  - Accepts search rules: target county/zip, min bed count, max purchase price, and yield threshold (e.g., >15% CoC).\n  - Queries Tavily API for newly indexed listings with keywords (\"hot tub\", \"price reduced\", \"seller financing\").\n  - Deduplicates incoming URLs against existing database records and queues newly discovered leads into the `INBOX` stage of the user\'s CRM pipeline.\n- [ ] **HOA \"Pencil Audit\" Analyzer (`POST /api/audit/analyze-doc`):**\n  - Handles multipart PDF uploads (CC&R bylaws, municipal STR regulations).\n  - Extracts text and sends full document context to Gemini 2.5 Flash with a strict JSON extraction schema:\n    * `str_status`: `\"PERMITTED\"` | `\"CONDITIONAL\"` | `\"PROHIBITED\"`\n    * `minimum_stay_days`: integer (0 if nightly allowed, 30 if restricted)\n    * `parking_limit_vehicles`: integer or string description\n    * `quiet_hours`: string description and decibel rules\n    * `amenity_fees`: string details on HOA pool/clubhouse charges\n    * `fines_schedule`: summary of violation penalties\n    * `citations`: array of `{ page_number: number, clause_section: string, exact_quote: string }`\n    * `risk_rating`: `\"LOW\"` | `\"MEDIUM\"` | `\"HIGH\"`\n\n#### 3. Client-Side Financial Underwriting Math Engine\n- [ ] Create a pure TypeScript underwriting utility (`calculateUnderwriteMetrics`) executing real-time client-side calculations:\n  - **Mortgage & Debt Service:**\n    - Conventional (standard 30-year amortization, custom down payment, closing costs).\n    - DSCR Loan: calculates required coverage:\n      $$\\text{DSCR} = \\frac{\\text{Monthly Gross Projected STR Revenue}}{\\text{Total Monthly PITI (Principal + Interest + Taxes + Insurance)}}$$\n      Includes dynamic status badges: Green ($\\ge 1.25$), Amber ($1.00 - 1.24$), Red ($< 1.00$).\n    - Creative / Seller Financing: support custom down payment, negotiated interest rate, interest-only period, and balloon payment horizon (e.g., 5-year balloon with 30-year amortization).\n    - Creative / Subject-To: support existing mortgage balance takeover + seller gap second note.\n  - **Expense Stack Calculation:**\n    - Property taxes, STR insurance, utilities, internet/tech stack, HOA fees.\n    - Variable expenses: Airbnb 3% host cut, turnover cleaning (passed through or net subsidized), property management fee (10\342\200\22320%), maintenance & Capex reserves (5\342\200\2238%).\n  - **KPI Returns:**\n    - Annualized Cash-on-Cash (CoC) Return.\n    - Net Operating Income (NOI) and Net Capitalization Rate (Cap Rate).\n    - Monthly Net Free Cash Flow.\n    - Break-Even Occupancy Percentage.\n  - **Live Sensitivity Stress Test:** Sliders to stress-test returns against $\\pm 20\\%$ shifts in Average Daily Rate (ADR) and $\\pm 15\\%$ drops in occupancy.\n\n#### 4. The Logged-In User Interface & Dashboard Architecture\n- [ ] **Global Dashboard Shell:**\n  - Sticky top bar with Breadcrumbs, Global Search (\"Search address, MLS ID, or market...\"), Deal Ingest Quick-Button (`+ Ingest Link`), and User / Demo Mode switcher.\n  - Collapsible Sidebar with links:\n    * `Deal Radar (Scanner)`\n    * `Pipeline CRM (Kanban)`\n    * `Underwriter Lab`\n    * `Pencil Audit (HOA & Legal)`\n    * `Portfolio (Pro Forma vs Actuals)`\n    * `Settings & API Keys`\n- [ ] **Screen 1: Pipeline CRM (Kanban Board):**\n  - Powered by `@dnd-kit/core`.\n  - Columns: `1. Scanned Inbox` $\\rightarrow$ `2. Underwriting` $\\rightarrow$ `3. Due Diligence` $\\rightarrow$ `4. Offer Sent` $\\rightarrow$ `5. Under Contract` $\\rightarrow$ `6. Acquired`.\n  - Cards show property image, address, purchase price, CoC %, DSCR badge, and HOA status dot.\n  - Dragging a card updates the status in the database with optimistic UI updates.\n  - Clicking any card slides out the comprehensive **Deal Detail Drawer**.\n- [ ] **Screen 2: Underwriter Lab & Deal Detail Drawer:**\n  - Split-screen layout:\n    * Left: Property photo gallery, specs, submarket seasonality bar chart (Recharts).\n    * Right: Interactive Financing Strategy Selector (`Conventional` | `DSCR` | `Seller Finance`), dynamic scrub-sliders for ADR and Occupancy, and expandable line-item expense drawers.\n  - Export Action: \"Download Lender Memo (PDF)\" \342\200\224 generates a clean, printable 1-page investment summary PDF complete with photos, capitalization stack, DSCR ratio, and sensitivity metrics.\n- [ ] **Screen 3: Pencil Audit Interface:**\n  - PDF drop-zone supporting direct drag-and-drop.\n  - Split audit view: PDF viewer on the left, AI Risk Scorecard and checklist on the right.\n  - Interactive citation badges: clicking a clause pin automatically jumps the PDF viewer to the highlighted page and section.\n- [ ] **Screen 4: Post-Acquisition Portfolio Dashboard (Pro Forma vs. Actuals):**\n  - Aggregate metrics across acquired properties: Total Net Cash Flow, Average Portfolio Occupancy, Total Debt Balance.\n  - Monthly bar/area charts comparing Underwritten Pro Forma Revenue vs. Realized Bank/Airbnb Payouts.\n  - Drag-and-drop CSV importer for Airbnb and Vrbo monthly payout sheets that automatically parses reservation income and cleaning fees without requiring enterprise PMS software.\n\n---\n\n### EXECUTION CHECKLIST FOR IMPLEMENTATION\n\n#### Sprint 1: Project Setup & Types\n- [ ] Initialize Vite + React 19 + TypeScript app with Tailwind CSS and `@shadcn/ui`.\n- [ ] Create `types/deal.ts` defining: `Deal`, `FinancingTerms`, `OperatingExpenses`, `AuditSummary`, and `PipelineStage`.\n- [ ] Implement pure underwriting calculations in `src/utils/underwriterMath.ts` and verify calculations against test unit fixtures.\n\n#### Sprint 2: State Management & Guest Demo Mode\n- [ ] Set up `useDealStore` using Zustand to manage deal lists, active filters, selected deal, and demo mode flags.\n- [ ] Create `src/mock/demoDeals.ts` containing the 3 pre-underwritten properties (Gatlinburg, Scottsdale, Gulf Shores) with full audit data, photo assets, and financials.\n- [ ] Build the Guest Demo entry toggle and Auth gate layout.\n\n#### Sprint 3: The Underwriter Component & Kanban CRM\n- [ ] Build the interactive `<UnderwritingCalculator />` with dynamic sliders and strategy tabs.\n- [ ] Build the drag-and-drop Kanban pipeline board using `@dnd-kit/core`.\n- [ ] Build the slide-out `<DealDrawer />` displaying comprehensive property data.\n\n#### Sprint 4: Backend Integration & AI Audit Services\n- [ ] Create backend routes for URL ingestion (`/api/deals/ingest-url`).\n- [ ] Connect Gemini 2.5 Flash structured output extraction to parse listing text and HOA documents.\n- [ ] Build the `<DocumentDropzone />` and `<AuditResultsCard />` displaying HOA parking, noise, and stay rules.\n\n#### Sprint 5: Portfolio Sync & PDF Export\n- [ ] Build CSV parser for Airbnb/Vrbo reservation downloads.\n- [ ] Build the Pro Forma vs. Actuals analytics view using `recharts`.\n- [ ] Implement client-side PDF export for 1-click Lender Investment Memos.\n\n---\n\nProceed with building the application step-by-step. Start by creating the complete TypeScript data models, financial math utility engine, and the 1-Click Guest Demo state manager.\n\n\nAdd Firebase to my app\n\nEnable Cloud SQL for project gen-lang-client-0199372874 in region us-east1\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nFirebase instructions: The user has successfully accepted Firebase terms. Set up Firebase using the following configurations.\nuser_confirmed_in_ui: true\nprojectID: alpine-vigil-5cf5x,gen-lang-client-0199372874\nfirebaseProduct: 1\nCloud SQL instructions: Set up Cloud SQL using the following configurations.\nregion: us-east1\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    items {
      text: "Act as a Principal Full-Stack Engineer and Architect. You are building the complete authenticated application and backend systems for \"PencilSTR\" \342\200\224 an institutional-grade Short-Term Rental (STR) acquisition, underwriting, and portfolio management platform.\n\nThe public landing page is already completed. Your objective is to build the full logged-in user experience, the guest demo environment, and the robust backend services that power them.\n\n---\n\n### TECH STACK & SYSTEM CONSTRAINTS\n- **Frontend:** React 19 + Vite (TypeScript), Tailwind CSS, `@shadcn/ui`, `lucide-react`, `recharts` for financial visualizations, `@dnd-kit/core` for the Kanban CRM board, and `zustand` for client state.\n- **Backend / Edge Layer:** Node.js (Express or Hono) or Python (FastAPI). Clean service-layer pattern with typed request/response schemas.\n- **Database & Auth:** Supabase (PostgreSQL with RLS), Supabase Auth, and Supabase Storage for PDF document uploads.\n- **AI & Extraction Agents:** Gemini 2.5 Flash (via API) utilizing Structured JSON outputs for data extraction and long-context PDF analysis.\n- **External Integration Stubs & Providers:** Firecrawl API (URL web scraping), RentCast API (assessor and market rent benchmarks), Tavily API (autonomous market searches).\n- **Design Language:** Precision Architectural Light Mode. Warm bone/alabaster canvas (`#FAF9F6`), crisp white surfaces (`#FFFFFF`), hairline borders (`#E5E4DF`), charcoal text (`#111110`), racing green return metrics (`#0B3B24`), and rich amber warnings (`#D97706`).\n\n---\n\n### CORE ARCHITECTURAL REQUIREMENTS\n\n#### 1. Dual-Mode Authentication & Instant Guest Demo\n- [ ] Implement seamless standard authentication via Supabase Auth (Magic Link, Email/Password, and Google OAuth).\n- [ ] Implement a **1-Click Guest Demo Mode** accessible from the login screen:\n  - Initializes a temporary session or isolated sandbox environment without requiring email or payment.\n  - Automatically hydrates the database/client state with 3 fully realized pre-modeled deals across different markets:\n    1. *The Ridge Alpine* (4-Bed Gatlinburg Cabin, DSCR-financed, 19.4% CoC, Unrestricted HOA).\n    2. *Kierland Hideaway* (5-Bed Scottsdale Luxury Villa with Pool, Conventional, 17.1% CoC, Strict Noise Rules).\n    3. *Gulf Shores Sandcastle* (6-Bed Beachfront, Seller Financed / Creative, 22.8% CoC, HOA vehicle limits).\n  - Guest sessions can test every feature (sliders, Kanban moves, HOA document uploads, PDF memo downloads) with volatile state preserved in session storage or an ephemeral guest user row.\n\n#### 2. Backend API Services & Integration Pipelines\n- [ ] **URL Ingestion Endpoint (`POST /api/deals/ingest-url`):**\n  - Accepts a raw property URL (Zillow, Redfin, or brokerage listing).\n  - Uses Firecrawl (or mock scraper fallback) to extract the webpage markdown.\n  - Passes extracted markdown to Gemini 2.5 Flash with a strict JSON Schema returning: street address, city, state, zip, list price, beds, baths, sqft, year built, listed HOA fees, tax estimates, and photo URLs.\n  - Queries RentCast API (or regional valuation baseline) for assessed tax records and submarket Long-Term / STR rent index.\n  - Persists the new record into Supabase and returns a fully populated `Deal` object.\n- [ ] **Autonomous Market Sweep Engine (`POST /api/scanner/run-sweep` & Scheduled Cron):**\n  - Accepts search rules: target county/zip, min bed count, max purchase price, and yield threshold (e.g., >15% CoC).\n  - Queries Tavily API for newly indexed listings with keywords (\"hot tub\", \"price reduced\", \"seller financing\").\n  - Deduplicates incoming URLs against existing database records and queues newly discovered leads into the `INBOX` stage of the user\'s CRM pipeline.\n- [ ] **HOA \"Pencil Audit\" Analyzer (`POST /api/audit/analyze-doc`):**\n  - Handles multipart PDF uploads (CC&R bylaws, municipal STR regulations).\n  - Extracts text and sends full document context to Gemini 2.5 Flash with a strict JSON extraction schema:\n    * `str_status`: `\"PERMITTED\"` | `\"CONDITIONAL\"` | `\"PROHIBITED\"`\n    * `minimum_stay_days`: integer (0 if nightly allowed, 30 if restricted)\n    * `parking_limit_vehicles`: integer or string description\n    * `quiet_hours`: string description and decibel rules\n    * `amenity_fees`: string details on HOA pool/clubhouse charges\n    * `fines_schedule`: summary of violation penalties\n    * `citations`: array of `{ page_number: number, clause_section: string, exact_quote: string }`\n    * `risk_rating`: `\"LOW\"` | `\"MEDIUM\"` | `\"HIGH\"`\n\n#### 3. Client-Side Financial Underwriting Math Engine\n- [ ] Create a pure TypeScript underwriting utility (`calculateUnderwriteMetrics`) executing real-time client-side calculations:\n  - **Mortgage & Debt Service:**\n    - Conventional (standard 30-year amortization, custom down payment, closing costs).\n    - DSCR Loan: calculates required coverage:\n      $$\\text{DSCR} = \\frac{\\text{Monthly Gross Projected STR Revenue}}{\\text{Total Monthly PITI (Principal + Interest + Taxes + Insurance)}}$$\n      Includes dynamic status badges: Green ($\\ge 1.25$), Amber ($1.00 - 1.24$), Red ($< 1.00$).\n    - Creative / Seller Financing: support custom down payment, negotiated interest rate, interest-only period, and balloon payment horizon (e.g., 5-year balloon with 30-year amortization).\n    - Creative / Subject-To: support existing mortgage balance takeover + seller gap second note.\n  - **Expense Stack Calculation:**\n    - Property taxes, STR insurance, utilities, internet/tech stack, HOA fees.\n    - Variable expenses: Airbnb 3% host cut, turnover cleaning (passed through or net subsidized), property management fee (10\342\200\22320%), maintenance & Capex reserves (5\342\200\2238%).\n  - **KPI Returns:**\n    - Annualized Cash-on-Cash (CoC) Return.\n    - Net Operating Income (NOI) and Net Capitalization Rate (Cap Rate).\n    - Monthly Net Free Cash Flow.\n    - Break-Even Occupancy Percentage.\n  - **Live Sensitivity Stress Test:** Sliders to stress-test returns against $\\pm 20\\%$ shifts in Average Daily Rate (ADR) and $\\pm 15\\%$ drops in occupancy.\n\n#### 4. The Logged-In User Interface & Dashboard Architecture\n- [ ] **Global Dashboard Shell:**\n  - Sticky top bar with Breadcrumbs, Global Search (\"Search address, MLS ID, or market...\"), Deal Ingest Quick-Button (`+ Ingest Link`), and User / Demo Mode switcher.\n  - Collapsible Sidebar with links:\n    * `Deal Radar (Scanner)`\n    * `Pipeline CRM (Kanban)`\n    * `Underwriter Lab`\n    * `Pencil Audit (HOA & Legal)`\n    * `Portfolio (Pro Forma vs Actuals)`\n    * `Settings & API Keys`\n- [ ] **Screen 1: Pipeline CRM (Kanban Board):**\n  - Powered by `@dnd-kit/core`.\n  - Columns: `1. Scanned Inbox` $\\rightarrow$ `2. Underwriting` $\\rightarrow$ `3. Due Diligence` $\\rightarrow$ `4. Offer Sent` $\\rightarrow$ `5. Under Contract` $\\rightarrow$ `6. Acquired`.\n  - Cards show property image, address, purchase price, CoC %, DSCR badge, and HOA status dot.\n  - Dragging a card updates the status in the database with optimistic UI updates.\n  - Clicking any card slides out the comprehensive **Deal Detail Drawer**.\n- [ ] **Screen 2: Underwriter Lab & Deal Detail Drawer:**\n  - Split-screen layout:\n    * Left: Property photo gallery, specs, submarket seasonality bar chart (Recharts).\n    * Right: Interactive Financing Strategy Selector (`Conventional` | `DSCR` | `Seller Finance`), dynamic scrub-sliders for ADR and Occupancy, and expandable line-item expense drawers.\n  - Export Action: \"Download Lender Memo (PDF)\" \342\200\224 generates a clean, printable 1-page investment summary PDF complete with photos, capitalization stack, DSCR ratio, and sensitivity metrics.\n- [ ] **Screen 3: Pencil Audit Interface:**\n  - PDF drop-zone supporting direct drag-and-drop.\n  - Split audit view: PDF viewer on the left, AI Risk Scorecard and checklist on the right.\n  - Interactive citation badges: clicking a clause pin automatically jumps the PDF viewer to the highlighted page and section.\n- [ ] **Screen 4: Post-Acquisition Portfolio Dashboard (Pro Forma vs. Actuals):**\n  - Aggregate metrics across acquired properties: Total Net Cash Flow, Average Portfolio Occupancy, Total Debt Balance.\n  - Monthly bar/area charts comparing Underwritten Pro Forma Revenue vs. Realized Bank/Airbnb Payouts.\n  - Drag-and-drop CSV importer for Airbnb and Vrbo monthly payout sheets that automatically parses reservation income and cleaning fees without requiring enterprise PMS software.\n\n---\n\n### EXECUTION CHECKLIST FOR IMPLEMENTATION\n\n#### Sprint 1: Project Setup & Types\n- [ ] Initialize Vite + React 19 + TypeScript app with Tailwind CSS and `@shadcn/ui`.\n- [ ] Create `types/deal.ts` defining: `Deal`, `FinancingTerms`, `OperatingExpenses`, `AuditSummary`, and `PipelineStage`.\n- [ ] Implement pure underwriting calculations in `src/utils/underwriterMath.ts` and verify calculations against test unit fixtures.\n\n#### Sprint 2: State Management & Guest Demo Mode\n- [ ] Set up `useDealStore` using Zustand to manage deal lists, active filters, selected deal, and demo mode flags.\n- [ ] Create `src/mock/demoDeals.ts` containing the 3 pre-underwritten properties (Gatlinburg, Scottsdale, Gulf Shores) with full audit data, photo assets, and financials.\n- [ ] Build the Guest Demo entry toggle and Auth gate layout.\n\n#### Sprint 3: The Underwriter Component & Kanban CRM\n- [ ] Build the interactive `<UnderwritingCalculator />` with dynamic sliders and strategy tabs.\n- [ ] Build the drag-and-drop Kanban pipeline board using `@dnd-kit/core`.\n- [ ] Build the slide-out `<DealDrawer />` displaying comprehensive property data.\n\n#### Sprint 4: Backend Integration & AI Audit Services\n- [ ] Create backend routes for URL ingestion (`/api/deals/ingest-url`).\n- [ ] Connect Gemini 2.5 Flash structured output extraction to parse listing text and HOA documents.\n- [ ] Build the `<DocumentDropzone />` and `<AuditResultsCard />` displaying HOA parking, noise, and stay rules.\n\n#### Sprint 5: Portfolio Sync & PDF Export\n- [ ] Build CSV parser for Airbnb/Vrbo reservation downloads.\n- [ ] Build the Pro Forma vs. Actuals analytics view using `recharts`.\n- [ ] Implement client-side PDF export for 1-click Lender Investment Memos.\n\n---\n\nProceed with building the application step-by-step. Start by creating the complete TypeScript data models, financial math utility engine, and the 1-Click Guest Demo state manager.\n\n\nAdd Firebase to my app\n\nEnable Cloud SQL for project gen-lang-client-0199372874 in region us-east1\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nFirebase instructions: The user has successfully accepted Firebase terms. Set up Firebase using the following configurations.\nuser_confirmed_in_ui: true\nprojectID: alpine-vigil-5cf5x,gen-lang-client-0199372874\nfirebaseProduct: 1\nCloud SQL instructions: Set up Cloud SQL using the following configurations.\nregion: us-east1\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
    }
  }
}
