    thinking: "**Initiating Architectural Design**\n\nOkay, I\'m diving into the architectural design for PencilSTR. I\'m focusing on the authenticated application and backend systems. Currently, I\'m mapping out the key components, considering scalability, security, and a robust user experience. The underwriting and financing aspects will be integral from the outset. I am now proceeding with the first drafts of the system-level design.\n\n\n**Defining User Experience & Backend**\n\nI\'ve clarified the tech stack. I\'m building the logged-in user experience, guest demo, and backend services. For the frontend, I\'m using React 19 with Vite, Tailwind CSS, `@shadcn/ui`, and more. I plan to use Supabase for the database, auth, and storage. Gemini 2.5 Flash will handle AI tasks, extracting data and analyzing PDFs. I also have several external APIs like Firecrawl and RentCast to integrate with.\n\n\n**Defining Authentication & APIs**\n\nI\'m now integrating seamless authentication using Supabase, including magic links and Google OAuth. The standout feature is the 1-Click Guest Demo, instantly providing a pre-populated sandbox with three diverse deals for testing all features. On the backend, I\'m building a URL ingestion endpoint. This API will take property URLs and use Firecrawl to extract data, feeding it to Gemini 2.5 Flash for structured data. RentCast will give tax data, and everything will be saved to Supabase.\n\n\n**Developing Automation Systems**\n\nI\'m now building the automation systems. I\'m focusing on the autonomous market sweep engine, which uses search rules and the Tavily API to find new listings. The incoming URLs are then checked and placed into the CRM pipeline. I\'m also working on the HOA \"Pencil Audit\" Analyzer. It will handle PDF uploads and extract text, sending it to Gemini 2.5 Flash for structured data extraction based on a strict JSON schema.\n\n\n**Refining Financial Modeling**\n\nI\'m now integrating dynamic status badges into the financial modeling, with clear indicators for deal viability. I\'m focusing on incorporating support for creative financing options like custom down payments, negotiated interest rates, and balloon payments. I\'m also ensuring the system can handle subject-to scenarios, including existing mortgage takeover with a seller gap second note. Next, I am working on the expense stack calculations. I will be including property taxes, STR insurance, utilities, and internet.\n\n\n"
