  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Current Directives**\n\nI\'m currently navigating a conflict in instructions. I see a reference to \"Beowulf Part 3\" in a previous prompt, but the latest directive asks me to act as a full-stack engineer building an authenticated application. This shift requires me to re-orient my processing. I need to prioritize the most recent instruction and determine how the previous one affects my current task, if at all.\n\n\n**Defining Backend Services**\n\nI\'m now focused on the backend systems for \"PencilSTR.\" The goal is to build the full logged-in user experience and backend services. I\'m prioritizing the tech stack: React 19, Vite, Tailwind CSS, and Supabase for the frontend, and Node.js (Express or Hono) or Python (FastAPI) for the backend. Supabase handles the database, auth, and storage, while AI agents with Gemini 2.5 Flash will handle data extraction.\n\n\n**Prioritizing User Authentication**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on dual-mode authentication, a core requirement. I will implement Supabase Auth for standard sign-in methods. Crucially, I\'m designing a 1-click guest demo. This instant access will feature pre-modeled deals: *The Ridge Alpine*, *Kierland Hideaway*, and *Gulf Shores Sandcastle*. Guest sessions allow testing all app features, with state held in session storage, without requiring sign-up. I will start the URL Ingestion Endpoint (`POST`).\n\n\n**Developing Data Ingestion**\n\nI\'m now focused on the data ingestion pipeline. I plan to use an API endpoint at `/api/deals/ingest-url` to handle raw property URLs. Firecrawl or a mock scraper will extract markdown from the webpages, then I\'ll use Gemini 2.5 Flash to extract data and validate it against a JSON schema. Finally, I will persist the data into Supabase, enrich it with external data, and return a `Deal` object.\n\n\n**Refining Deal Risk Factors**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed risk factors into the deal objects, specifically `minimum_stay_days`, `parking_limit_vehicles`, `quiet_hours`, `amenity_fees`, `fines_schedule`, `citations`, and a `risk_rating`. My focus is on parsing and representing this information accurately. I\'m prioritizing data structure and data type consistency across all the data fields for each property. The risk rating will be crucial for the client-side underwriting engine.\n\n\n\n**Modeling Financial Scenarios**\n\nI\'m now diving into financial modeling, focusing on various return metrics and sensitivities for the properties. I\'m calculating Unlevered and Levered Cash-on-Cash Return, Capitalization Rate, Net Operating Income, and monthly Net Cash Flow. I will create a sensitivity matrix to model Occupancy and ADR. I plan to use interactive sliders for purchase price, interest rates, down payments, and other inputs for detailed projections.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 940480201
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
    provider_assigned_message_id: "8Hy5aseTEcfQz7IPmpmP2QM"
  }
}
