  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Constructing Server.ts**\n\nI\'m starting by building the `server.ts` file from scratch, aiming for a robust, production-ready Express server. My current focus is integrating `vite.middlewares` within dev mode. This should allow a smooth serving of both the backend API endpoints and the frontend Vite application via port 3000. I need to make sure this works correctly.\n\n\n**Verifying Vite Server Setup**\n\nI\'m now verifying the setup for `server.ts` with Vite, specifically in Vite 8 and 6, looking at how the middleware integrates. I\'m checking the routing for API endpoints, along with the fallback strategy for the frontend in both development and production. The example provided shows how it should be implemented.\n\n\n**Validating Deployment Strategies**\n\nI\'m now assessing various deployment configurations. I need to guarantee the client operates smoothly whether run through Vite directly or via `server.ts`. Client-side fallbacks for network issues are also critical. I\'m reviewing `package.json` scripts, specifically `\"dev\"` and `\"start\"`, and comparing `\"build\"` options. I\'ll need to define all the components systematically, starting with the deal types.\n\n\n**Defining Deal Types**\n\nI am now focusing on defining deal types, specifically for seller-financed properties with HOA considerations. I am planning the `HoaAuditReport` structure with clear status options, limits, and potential fines. I am designing a `User` type for authentication, incorporating guest demos and diverse auth methods. I\'m also preparing for the client-side state store in `zustand`, planning out `User`, `deals`, and tab navigation.\n\n\n**Designing State Management**\n\nI\'m now outlining the client-side state store using `zustand`, with the goal of managing the app\'s UI state and deal data. I\'m focusing on defining the structure, including booleans for modal visibility, view modes, underwriting overrides, and auth-related functions. I\'m prioritizing methods like `loginAsGuest()`, `login()`, `logout()`, and functions to manage deal state like `updateDealStage` and `addDeal`, while working towards integrating the authentication methods.\n\n\n**Calculating Financial Metrics**\n\nI\'m now calculating real-time returns and building a sensitivity matrix for short-term rental properties, focusing on dynamic cash-on-cash return, cap rate, and net operating income. I\'m also including a 5x5 dynamic grid to test occupancy versus ADR with color-coded yield heatmaps. Additionally, I\'m integrating a 5-year pro forma with annual appreciation, revenue, and expense inflation.\n\n\n**Refining Deal Card Display**\n\nI am now concentrating on refining the display for deal cards within the application. I\'m focusing on the `UNDER_CONTRACT`, `CLOSED`, and `ARCHIVED` statuses, and I am designing a visual layout that provides key information at a glance. I\'m prioritizing the display of property details, key financial metrics like CoC%, Cap Rate, and DSCR, as well as the HOA status. The aim is to create a design to enable quick stage advancement.\n\n**Building Auth Modal**\n\nI\'m currently working on an authentication modal in `src/components/AuthModal.tsx`. I\'m designing a clean, light mode interface with a prominent \"1-Click Instant Guest Demo\" option. This button will provide immediate access to a sandbox environment with pre-modeled deals. I\'ll also integrate standard Supabase authentication with email functionality for user login.\n\n\n**Implementing Authentication Flows**\n\nI\'m now integrating password login/signup, magic link authentication, and a Google OAuth button, while simultaneously incorporating security badges and an institutional disclaimer.\n\\n\\n\n**Developing URL Ingestion Modal**\n\nI am now building the `IngestUrlModal.tsx`. I\'ve added a Zillow/Redfin/Brokerage URL input, displaying a live Firecrawl scraping simulation. This progresses through Gemini 2.5 Flash parsing, RentCast comps retrieval, and deal hydration. I\'ve also pre-populated test URLs for one-click testing.\n\n\n**Constructing Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now building out the data structures for ordinance and CC&R analysis within the new studio components. I\'m focusing on parsing PDF documents or text, leveraging Gemini 2.5 Flash for accurate JSON extraction based on a strict schema that I\'m currently designing. The structures include status, limits, fees, and risk assessments for a dynamic audit report. I am incorporating a risk rating system, citations, and status badges.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 118204699
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
